<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-optimization-approximation" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Optimization and Approximation</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      This chapter finishes what derivatives can do for us, before we turn to integrals.
      It is built around three questions:
      <ul>
        <li><p>How do we find the <em>best possible</em> outcome? (<xref ref="sec-4-7-optimization"/>)</p></li>
        <li><p>How do we solve an equation that has <em>no formula</em>? (<xref ref="sec-4-8-newtons-method"/>)</p></li>
        <li><p>If we know a rate of change, can we <em>recover</em> the original quantity? (<xref ref="sec-4-9-antiderivatives"/>)</p></li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
      That last question is the doorway to the rest of the course. Keep an eye on it.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="./sec-4-7-optimization.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./sec-4-8-newtons-method.ptx"/>

  <xi:include href="./sec-4-9-antiderivatives.ptx"/>

</chapter>
